data.content:
## What Changed (Microsoft.OpenApi v1 → v2)

The `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` 10.0 package depends on **Microsoft.OpenApi v2**, which targets OpenAPI 3.1 and has major breaking changes:

| .NET 9 (OpenApi v1) | .NET 10 (OpenApi v2) |
|---|---|
| `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any.*` types (`OpenApiString`, etc.) | Removed — use `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode` |
| `schema.Nullable = true/false` | Removed — use `JsonSchemaType` flags with `JsonSchemaType.Null` |
| `schema.Example` (`IOpenApiAny`) | Now `JsonNode?` |
| `new OpenApiSecurityScheme { Reference = ... }` | Use `OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("id")` |
| `ReferenceType` enum on `OpenApiReference` | Reference types are now dedicated classes in `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References` |

## Fixed Code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        // IOpenApiAny → JsonNode
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    // OpenApiSecurityScheme + OpenApiReference → OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference
    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
            {
                // .Nullable removed — clear the Null flag from the Type enum
                property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
            }
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

### Summary of fixes

1. **`OpenApiString` → `JsonValue.Create(...)`** — remove `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any`, add `using System.Text.Json.Nodes`.
2. **`OpenApiSecurityScheme { Reference = new OpenApiReference { ... } }`** → single-line `new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2")` (from `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References`).
3. **`property.Value.Nullable = false`** → `property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null` to strip the null type from the flags enum.
